  "notes": [
    "The SGX-GETH attestation proxy's creation receipt emitted its only Upgraded event, selecting AutomataDcapV3Attestation 0x5e46443bd131eb6d4c6fb4849bad29af9596dd72, which stayed active with an unchanged runtime through the exploit.",
    "Upgraded event selecting AutomataDcapV3Attestation 0x5f73f0adc7daa6134fe751c4a78d524f9384e0b5, the SGX-RETH attestation implementation active through the exploit.",
    "Exact L1 depletion of the Taiko Bridge (native ETH) and ERC20Vault (ERC-20 Transfer logs) caused by forged messages across 36 transactions, including 18 ETH taken as the processing fee by 0xc0ffeebabe while it front-ran the forged message 9000. Each asset is valued at its DefiLlama price nearest its first release. The reported DefiLlama figure is $1.7M (source-12). Recoveries are not deducted.",
    "The exploit also required the leaked enclave signing key (offchain); admission rests on the onchain attestation defect, without which a DEBUG quote could not register.",
    "Same missing local-report attribute check in the SGX-RETH attestation; both SGX sub-proofs were needed, and target-1's later activation supplies the knot."
  ]
